#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:5
#: 8379dc4ad90341479a8900fa23744ff5
msgid "Adding a New Parameter to Copter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:7
#: 579921ca6e734235ac38a1febb06c703
msgid "Parameters can either be part of the main code or part of a library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:10
#: 4541e5cb43fb43079db796157f66691e
msgid "Adding a parameter to the main code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:12
#: 51c04d2656d34a6cbc9760aba305615a
msgid "**Step #1:** Find a spare slot in the Parameters class's enum in `Parameters.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Parameters.h>`__ and add your new parameter as shown below in red.  Some things to be careful of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:17
#: e20ef7cb56c241a1b46b2644f7858015
msgid "Try to add the parameter close to parameters that share a similar function or worst case add to the end of the \"Misc\" section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:19
#: c0d5cb38c7c14fdeac654b3bf1bb87c0
msgid "Ensure that the section you are adding it to is not full.  You can check if the section is full by counting the number of parameters in the section and ensuring that the last element is less than the next sections first element.  I.e. the Misc section's first parameter is #20.  my_new_parameter is #36.  If the next section began at #36 we would not be able to add the new parameter here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:25
#: d3c72f585d5349a094a3082d10bc2d75
msgid "Do not add a parameter in the middle of a group thus causing the slots for existing parameters to change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:27
#: 05c179d416164b0f83720e4cd3572f91
msgid "Do not use slots with \"deprecated\" or \"remove\" comments beside them because some users may still have the defaults for these old parameters in their eeprom so your new parameter's default value could be set strangely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:61
#: 108c9a48871c47c4a8563fcbb8aeeaa9
msgid "**Step #2:** Declare the variable within the Parameters class somewhere below the enum.  Possible types include AP_Int8, AP_Int16, AP_Float, AP_Int32 and AP_Vector3 (Note: unsigned integers are not currently supported).  The name of the variable should be the same as the new enum but with the \"k_param\\_\" prefix removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:99
#: 0562146714d246c6bf955bf7ff2b99cb
msgid "**Step #3:** Add the variable declaration to the var_info table in `Parameters.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Parameters.cpp>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:111
#: 684ba9f9c15c4842bf4213d8827aa7e2
msgid "The @Param ~ @User comments are used by the ground station (i.e. Mission Planner) to display advice to the user and limit the values that the user may set the parameter to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:115
#: 47f42e18024a4156ad12ba5050fe04f8
msgid "The parameter name (i.e. \"MY_NEW_PARAMETER\") is limited to 16 characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:118
#: f669f72fa98544caa4453143af68a0db
msgid "**Step #4:** Add the parameters default to `config.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/config.h>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:127
#: 8ca3b977148c4f9aaa533d0be84123b8
msgid "You're done!  The new parameter can be access from the main code (not the libraries) as g.my_new_parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:130
#: 004765f478fe46a49c368c3b10e5bae1
msgid "ArduPilot vehicle's global parameter classes are crowded. To avoid exceeding the maximum number of parameters in a vehicle's Parameter class, another class for global parameters (named 'ParametersG2') has been introduced. Adding parameters to this class is similar to adding parameters in libraries. The parameters added to this class can similarly be accessed from within the vehicle's main code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:133
#: 121054c084ab403685324ad1aed3b3c6
msgid "Adding a parameter to a library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:135
#: b472bbcdeaee4a16bf77e1d8318fd947
msgid "Parameters can also be added to libraries by following these steps which use the `AP_Compass <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_Compass>`__ library as an example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:139
#: ac3af28c4e6e44f2a63d0bbce4518082
msgid "**Step #1:** Add the new class variable to the top level .h file (i.e. `Compass.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Compass/AP_Compass.h>`__). Possible types include AP_Int8, AP_Int16, AP_Float, AP_Int32 and AP_Vector3f.  Also add the default value you'd like for the parameter (we will use this in step #2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:172
#: 7c9010e4507c434b9ddf172b60032088
msgid "**Step #2:**\\ Add the variable to the var_info table in the .cpp file (i.e. `Compass.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Compass/AP_Compass.cpp>`__) including @Param ~ @Increment comments to allow the GCS to display the description to the user and to control the min and max values set from the ground station.  When adding the new parameter be careful that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:178
#: 55a50c1dd69041deae9777e137dcc9da
msgid "The slot (i.e. \"9\" below) is one higher than the previous variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:180
#: dee3d17f89f541c29ae02b662a3af7a9
msgid "the parameter's name (i.e. MY_NEW_P) length is less than 16 including the object's prefix that will be added.  I.e. the compass object's prefix is \"COMPASS\\_\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:213
#: 1f0e6e78696344aab3c4b4ede1c751dc
msgid "The parameter can be accessed from within the library as \\_my_new_lib_parameter.  Note that we made the parameter \"protected\" so it cannot be access from outside the class.  If we'd made it public then it would have been accessible to the main code as well as \"compass._my_new_lib_parameter\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:219
#: 51ed432becb04f93949d09462ca464bb
msgid "**Step #3:** Add a declaration for var_info to the public section of the .h file of new library class in addition to the definition in the .cpp file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:225
#: dde47dabed55480d8348a6db53d238e9
msgid "**Step #4:** If the class is a completely new addition to the code (as opposed to an existing class like AP_Compass), it should be added to the main vehicle's var_info table in the `Parameters.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Parameters.cpp>`__ file (its order in the var_info table is not important).  Below in red where the Compass class appears."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:254
#: 5bb70653dc7c403d90fb6af83be18ebb
msgid "**Step #5:** If the class is a completely new addition to the code, also add k_param_my_new_lib to the enum in `Parameters.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Parameters.h>`__, where my_new_lib is the first argument to the GOBJECT declaration in `Parameters.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Parameters.cpp>`__. Read the comments above the enum to understand where to place the new value, as order is important here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:259
#: 0a3ee0ac4a6248a696922c6bb5e95428
msgid "Changing the type of a parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:261
#: 2f6728cc5d9c40d49f25926c69e51527
msgid "From time to time parameters need to be altered or renamed. ArduPilot has capabilities that allow this to be managed from release to release so that upgrades always preserve user configured parameters. Parameters are keyed off slots in the eeprom, so if the occupied slot does not change then the parameter does not change - regardless of its name. If however the type needs to change then the parameter needs to be moved to a new slot and the existing slot be reserved to prevent unexpected configuration. In order for the configuration to be preserved it needs to be copied and converted from the old slot to the new slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:263
#: 3431ef41523147fe918a2407a7292c09
msgid "**Step #1:** Change the index of the existing parameter to an unused index and add a comment to the effect that the old slot is reserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:265
#: d1b0d62b96654e2faccf5833f3849022
msgid "**Step #2:** In order to figure out the keys for conversion:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:267
#: 80cb759dd1b1409784b58d37475948ac
msgid "Set the AP_PARAM_KEY_DUMP definition to \"1\" `here in AP_Param.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Param/AP_Param.h#L36>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:269
#: d756e682a6d04a449648a61ccbeccfd8
msgid "Start the old code in SITL and all the parameter names and their magic numbers will be displayed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:271
#: 35d9e9dfee9041d6ba637f152c4458c5
msgid "Copy-paste from Copter's Parameters.cpp file's `existing parameter conversion tables like the ones done for the attitude controller gains <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Parameters.cpp#L1247>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:274
#: 6c37cc9ac2fb484e94abae7ee3271776
msgid "Parameter Conversion Expiration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:276
#: 833136c968464551be565b686d5a9165
msgid "Parameter conversions are necessary to ensure continuity for users as they upgrade to newer versions of ArduPilot.  However, the conversion process does utilise some resources on boot and does add to the flash cost of the code. Therefore we don't keep the conversion code forever more. To make it easier to find and remove the conversions, please add the following as a comment above any parameter conversion that you add:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-parameter.rst:283
#: 200f5591f50b4e4f81b12ea4b4f4555c
msgid "Please use the date format shown above to avoid ambiguity.  Please also keep the date on the same line as the key word \"PARAMETER_CONVERSION\" so that the date can be seen in the return, when grep-ing/searching the code.  When adding to an already existing AP_Param::ConversionInfo table, please add the conversions as a new block with the conversion comment above the new block.  For example:"
msgstr ""
